How an On-the-Fly System Works (Step-by-Step)
Instead of pulling a full question object from a database, your system follows a loop entirely on the user's device or via a quick API call:
[Student selects Skill] 
        ↓
[Engine runs JavaScript Template] → Generates random a, b, c variables
        ↓
[Math calculations run] ---------→ Solves the equation + generates wrong choices
        ↓
[UI Components render] ----------→ Renders text, inputs, and canvas graphs
        ↓
[Student submits answer] --------→ Validates user input against calculated answer
The Component Architecture You Need
To handle this cleanly as a solo dev, structure your code into three small parts per skill:
The Generator Script: A pure math file that picks random numbers, makes sure they are clean integers (e.g., ensuring square roots don't result in messy decimals unless intended), and returns an active data model.
The View Layer: A reusable UI container component (like GraphCanvas or MultipleChoiceGrid) that accepts the data model and renders it visually.
The Validator: A function that receives what the user typed or dragged and checks it against the true mathematical result.
